# Testing Rules

## Required with every implementation

- Write tests alongside code, not after.
- Cover happy path and legacy validation failures.
- Cover authorization/role checks when the source module has them.
- Cover multi-step / transaction flows when the source module has them.

## Evidence required before PASS

- Tests for the scoped change run and pass.
- Legacy vs New table lists each compared behavior as PASS or FAIL.
- FAIL or Unknown items block calling the module done.

## Do not

- Skip tests because the change is "small"
- Assert invented behavior not present in `source-app/` or `docs/`
- Mark PASS when tests were not run
